  "todaysTip": "Today's Tip",
  "homeTip1": "During flood season, boil drinking water for at least 1 minute. Keep ORS in stock to prevent waterborne illness.",
  "homeTip2": "Close windows and doors before a storm arrives. Cover them with thick cloth to guard against flying glass.",
  "homeTip3": "In an earthquake, get under a table and move away from walls. Never use the lift.",
  "homeTip4": "In a fire, stay low to the ground to keep below the smoke. Smoke always rises.",
  "homeTip5": "In summer heat, drink water every 30 minutes. Wear light-coloured clothing to avoid heatstroke.",
  "homeTip6": "Make ORS at home for diarrhoea: mix 1 teaspoon sugar and half a teaspoon salt into 1 litre of boiled, cooled water.",
  "homeTip7": "For a snakebite, keep the bitten area below heart level. Never cut it with a knife or scissors.",
  "homeTip8": "Before entering floodwater, disconnect electrical equipment. Move gas cylinders and lighters well away.",
  "homeTip9": "If an earthquake catches you outdoors, stay in the open — keep clear of trees and electricity poles.",
  "homeTip10": "If a fire starts indoors, leave calmly in single file. If there is heavy smoke, hold a wet cloth over your face.",
  "homeTip11": "Children dehydrate quickly in heat. Give them water first and sit them in the shade.",
  "homeTip12": "Caught outside in a severe storm, lie flat on low ground. Do not stand beside trees.",
  "homeTip13": "Keep at least 3 days of drinking water and dry food per household. Store separate water for washing.",
  "homeTip14": "Keep a first-aid kit at home: bandages, antiseptic, paracetamol, ORS sachets.",
  "homeTip15": "After a flood, never use pond water directly. Purify it by boiling or with chlorine tablets.",
  "homeTip16": "After an earthquake, do not go inside until the damaged parts of the building have been checked.",
  "homeTip17": "For fever, sponge the body with a wet cloth and drink plenty of water. Above 40°C, go to hospital.",
  "homeTip18": "During a sea storm, stay away from the coast. If the waves look abnormal, move to high ground at once.",
  "homeTip19": "In an electrical emergency, never touch a switch with wet hands. Keep rubber shoes on.",
